{%- comment -%}
  giscus: comments backed by GitHub Discussions in this repo. Gated on the
  `comments` flag, the way the old Disqus include was.

  Mapping is `specific` with `page.url` as the term, not the documented default
  of `pathname`. Under a path prefix the browser's pathname is `/blog/2016/06/x/`
  but at the custom domain it is `/2016/06/x/`, so pathname mapping would file
  the same post's comments under two different discussions across the Phase 9
  cutover. `page.url` carries no prefix and is stable across both.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if comments %}
<section class="comments" aria-label="Comments">
  <h2 class="comments-heading">Comments</h2>
  <script src="https://giscus.app/client.js"
          data-repo="dwalend/blog"
          data-repo-id="MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkyMTg4NDk5NA=="
          data-category="Announcements"
          data-category-id="DIC_kwDOAU3wQs4DEDUY"
          data-mapping="specific"
          data-term="{{ page.url }}"
          data-strict="1"
          data-reactions-enabled="1"
          data-emit-metadata="0"
          data-input-position="top"
          data-theme="preferred_color_scheme"
          data-lang="en"
          data-loading="lazy"
          crossorigin="anonymous"
          async>
  </script>
  <noscript>
    <p class="comments-fallback">
      Comments need JavaScript. They live in
      <a href="https://github.com/dwalend/blog/discussions">this repo's GitHub Discussions</a>,
      which you can read and post to directly.
    </p>
  </noscript>
</section>
{%- endif %}
